	<groupId>com.chaconne-ai</groupId>
	<artifactId>openspreader</artifactId>
	<version>1.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
	<name>openspreader</name>
	<description>
		Multi-process programming components for Spring Boot: distributed locks,
		semaphores, latches, barriers, exchangers, a process pool, a replicated cache
		with Bloom filters, cluster-wide scheduling, RPC, MapReduce-style aggregation
		and DAG orchestration, all on the embedded spreader cluster.

		Each component keeps the shape of its java.util.concurrent counterpart but spans
		every instance of the application instead of one JVM: a ProcessingMutex is
		acquired and released like a ReentrantLock. The cluster runs inside the same JVM
		as the application's beans, so there is no Redis, no ZooKeeper and no broker.
		Every component has two scopes, one confined to a single application and one
		spanning the cluster. The cache replicates operations rather than data and every
		node holds a full replica, so reads never leave the process.

		Nothing is enabled by default: each component is switched on through properties,
		so adding this starter to a running service changes nothing until one is asked for.

		Inherited limits, stated rather than hidden: election is pre-emptive rather than
		consensus-based, so under a network partition two sides can each hold a leader,
		and the cache is memory only.
	</description>
